# Keep the build context small and free of local state.
#
# This file exists because Dockerfile line 23 is `COPY . .`. Without this, Docker
# uploads the entire working directory to the builder -- including .git (the whole
# history), .kamal/secrets, node_modules and any .env on this machine.
#
# Nothing here is a secret in the strict sense, but two consequences are real:
#
#   1. .env is read by Next.js at BUILD time. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables get
#      inlined into the client bundle, so a RAILS_API_URL-style value is safe --
#      but any NEXT_PUBLIC_ value added to .env would ship to browsers.
#   2. The final image only carries .next/standalone, .next/static and public
#      (Dockerfile 68-74), so none of this reaches the pushed ECR image. It does
#      land in the intermediate build stage and in the local build cache, which
#      is still more persistence than anyone wants for local files.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: package.json, package-lock.json, next.config.ts,
# tsconfig.json, postcss.config.mjs, eslint.config.mjs, config/, src/, public/.
# The build needs all of them.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and history
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
.kamal
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
